        "original_id": "06d0e4b3-8c05-5fb6-82f2-5a7ea7f8e465",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patricia Veryan, Patricia Valeria Bannister\n- Works: A Company of Swans, A Song for Summer, A Countess Below Stairs, The Reluctant Heiress, The Morning Gift\n- Topics: book dedications, reissues, historical romance fiction, young adult market\n\nFacts:\n- Patricia Valeria Bannister was born on November 21, 1923, in London, England.\n- Patricia Veryan was the pen name of Patricia Valeria Bannister, who was a writer of historical romance fiction from 1978 until 2002.\n- Patricia Veryan died on November 18, 2009, in Bellevue, Washington, USA.\n- The book A Company of Swans is dedicated to Patricia Veryan.\n- A Song for Summer and four other novels—A Countess Below Stairs, A Company of Swans, The Reluctant Heiress, and The Morning Gift—were reissued between 2007 and 2009 for the young adult market.",
